const faq = [
  {
    "q": "What size should a JD main image be?",
    "a": "The most commonly published figure is 800 by 800 pixels at a 1:1 ratio, stated by nine of the ten pages that give a JD main image floor, collected on 10 September 2026. Tmall comes back the same. This is a modal value from published sources, not a figure read from JD, so confirm it in your seller backend."
  },
  {
    "q": "Are JD and Tmall image requirements the same?",
    "a": "Mostly. Published sources agree the two platforms match on the 800 by 800 floor, the 1:1 ratio, JPG and PNG formats and the five-image carousel. The one difference that holds is the white-background image, first on JD and fifth on Tmall. The widely repeated detail-width difference is a comparison between two sources, not two platforms."
  },
